1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
Rush China's highest highway and it'll put you on oxygen. I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:05,100
The G219 runs about 2,900 km, Xinjiang to Tibet.

3
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,600
It averages over 4,500 metres — for days on end.

4
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,000
915 kilometres of it sit above 4,000 metres.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,500
Its passes climb past 5,300 — five peaks over 5,000.

6
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:15,100
Fuel and help can be hundreds of kilometres apart.

7
00:00:15,100 --> 00:00:17,600
Double-tap if you'd still drive the whole thing.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,200
Climb too fast and altitude sickness is the real danger.

9
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:22,800
★ Expert Tip: take three days to go up, not one.

10
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:25,600
World's highest road — bucket list, or too far? You tell me.
